  "description": "VIZZOW crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 41 21 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C156 H181 Cl7 Dy6 N12 O12,3(C1 H4 O1),8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.501-3.522 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.15-97.60°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6L2(μ3-OH)3(μ3-O)(μ2-Cl)3Cl4(H2O)2]·3CH3OH·8H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
